        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What's the time limit?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>A generous 7-hour course limit, with a rolling sweep behind the final runner. Aid stations stay open the full window.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Is the course really a legal Boston qualifier?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. The route is USATF-certified and meets B.A.A. requirements, with a net elevation drop well within the allowable limit. Your time counts.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Can I defer or transfer my entry?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>One free deferral to the following year is allowed until 30 days out. Transfers to another runner are supported through the official portal until August 20.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Are there pacers?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Official pace groups run from 3:00 through 4:30 in 15-minute bands, plus dedicated qualifying-time pacers for the most common BQ standards.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What's included with my entry?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Chip timing, finisher medal, technical shirt, on-course nutrition, gear check, finish-line festival access, and your B.A.A.-ready certificate.</p></div></div>
      </>}
